 "imp-f-99-me-r-giment-d-infanterie-assaut-du-portique": {
  "imdbID": "tt1740461",
  "imdbRating": "5.1",
  "imdbVotes": "81",
  "Poster": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BZWE2NjQyNzAtZjBkNC00ZjVlLWIyZDItYTA1ZWMxMTk5NGE0XkEyXkFqcGdeQXVyMjM5NTI4Mzc@._V1_SX300.jpg",
  "Ratings": [
   {
    "Source": "Internet Movie Database",
    "Value": "5.1/10"
   }
  ],
  "Plot": "The soldiers climb ropes, first one rank of them, then another in this Lumiere film from 1897.The Lumieres recognized, as few other film makers clearly did at this stage, that the movie audience was able to process more than one set of movements. Some of their most striking works from this period show three separate sorts of movement taking place in different areas of the frame. Basically, there was always something else for the audience to look at once it had taken in what had happened in one portion of the frame. It looked at something new and then could return.In this we see three sets of movement: as each rank moves to the ropes, as they climb them, and as they exit to the left. Despite the dozen or so soldiers, there isn't that much for the eye to follow."
 },
 "imp-f-a-bord-du-formidable-escrime-au-sabre": {
  "imdbID": "tt1741490",
  "imdbRating": "5.3",
  "imdbVotes": "90",
  "Poster": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BY2RjZDcwMjAtODAzYi00NzMxLWI3NjEtMzllNDQ3ZDc2ODY5XkEyXkFqcGc@._V1_SX300.jpg",
  "Ratings": [
   {
    "Source": "Internet Movie Database",
    "Value": "5.3/10"
   }
  ],
  "Plot": "A bord du 'Formidable': escrime au sabre (1896)A small group of men are doing a few tricks with swords. That's basically what you see in this early actuality film from the Lumiere company. Obviously if you're wanting to see something ground-breaking then you're not going to witness that here. With that said, this is a rather bland film even for an actuality. There's just nothing overly entertaining that you're looking at and the men's sword play just doesn't do much for you. In fact, I'd argue that this here is one of the weaker films that I've seen from the Lumiere Brothers.This and other films from the Lumiere Brothers can be seen online at various sites including YouTube."
 },
