  "Plot": "Alger: place du gouvernement (1896) The title pretty much tells you what you need to know about this actuality film from the Lumiere Brothers. The camera is stationed in front of what I'm guessing is a government building in Alger. There's really not too much that happens here and to my knowledge there's no important government official that we can see. It's basically just a snap shot from outside the building. I guess people at the time might have been interested in seeing the building and today's viewers might enjoy the film for the same reason. One just really shouldn't expect much of anything else."
