  "Plot": "Attack on a Piquet (1899) This U.K. film from R.W. Paul has a group of soldiers sitting behind a bush when another group comes up from being them, shooting them and then walking off. This war picture certainly isn't going to be mistaken for some sort of masterpiece but it's entertaining for what it is. The thing clocks in at just thirty seconds so obviously you shouldn't be expecting anything like a plot. Everything is pretty simple as we see the men sitting and then getting shot. The camera position was quite good and it perfectly captured all the action, which is the best thing that can be said."
