 "imp-f-evian-embarquement": {
  "imdbID": "tt2459010",
  "imdbRating": "4.3",
  "imdbVotes": "114",
  "Poster": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BY2ExMTExNWEtMzU2OC00ZGExLWFlNzItNWM1OTU3NGIyZWZiXkEyXkFqcGdeQXVyMjM5NTI4Mzc@._V1_SX300.jpg",
  "Ratings": [
   {
    "Source": "Internet Movie Database",
    "Value": "4.3/10"
   }
  ],
  "Plot": "Embarquement (1896) This film from the Lumiere Brothers captures a group of people entering a ferry boat. At just under a minute that's pretty much what you see for the entire time. There's obviously nothing ground-breaking about this movie and it certainly didn't change film history but at the same time it's mildly entertaining simply because it just captures a moment in time. I'm sure those entering the ferry never thought that this movie would be seen by people over a hundred years later but it's always fascinating to watch these and just see the type of clothing people were wearing as well as seeing other things like the ships, crates and so on."
 },
