 "imp-f-paris-arc-de-triomphe": {
  "imdbID": "tt1672821",
  "imdbRating": "4.9",
  "imdbVotes": "110",
  "Poster": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BOTgxMzZhNDAtYWUyOC00NzM4LWE4NGUtODA4NTVlYTQxOTIxXkEyXkFqcGdeQXVyMjA0NzcwMjI@._V1_SX300.jpg",
  "Ratings": [
   {
    "Source": "Internet Movie Database",
    "Value": "4.9/10"
   }
  ],
  "Plot": "Paris, Arc de Triomphe (1896) This actuality film from the Lumiere Brothers certainly didn't change history or anything but it's mildly entertaining thanks in large part to it showing an actual Paris street back in 1896. The camera stays in one spot as various people and carriages go by. Yes, that's all that happens here but if you're a fan of these actuality movies then you'll be entertained by this one since we get some great visuals. Plus, it's fascinating getting to see an actual street in Paris. Hollywood has done movies set in Paris during this era but their re-created magic just can't compare to the real thing."
 },
