 "imp-f-paris-cort-ge-du-boeuf-gras-char-du-prince-du-carnaval": {
  "imdbID": "tt1740532",
  "imdbRating": "5.5",
  "imdbVotes": "103",
  "Poster": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/M/MV5BYTc2NjMwNWYtNTg0Yi00OGNlLTk0NWQtNjVjOWFiNDQyMWQxXkEyXkFqcGdeQXVyMjM5NTI4Mzc@._V1_SX300.jpg",
  "Ratings": [
   {
    "Source": "Internet Movie Database",
    "Value": "5.5/10"
   }
  ],
  "Plot": "Paris, cortège du boeuf gras: Char du prince du carnaval (1897) This actuality film from the Lumiere Brothers has a camera stationed high up as it captures portions of a parade that is going on. We get to see quite a few people and various acts but the highlight happens right at the start when a large float, being drawn by horses, goes by the camera. This here is certainly the highlight and it makes the film worth sitting through. This clocks in at less than a minute so it's entertaining enough for what it is. Plus it's always fascinating getting to see things for how they really were back in the day. Fans of these actuality films should certainly enjoy this one."
 },
